  "full_text": "So God said the best religion was the one that had the most new vistas of understanding over a lifetime. The best religion is the one that has the most new. So somebody thought I spoiled communion. Yeah, sorry about that. I don't have the final answer. Here's what happens. Something changes in your life, and then you look back, then you look at things differently. We have a new sacrament, which is, well, I don't know if I want to be doing that. God said not to do it. He said it was like communion preparation. Before receiving communion, you're supposed to meditate. Not meditate. You're supposed to, I don't know, prepare yourself. I don't know what they say. I guess that's important, whatever their policy is. So you're supposed to prepare your heart. Anyway, so, and if you don't, it's a mortal sin or something like that. People start dying. Anyway, so God said, it's not a mortal sin. He said, I don't know, it's like communion preparation.",
